body:
No Sending comes. On a stone at the side of the road there is an apple core and a single black feather, and nobody.

The crows that follow the Witness have not followed her this year. You see them everywhere now, sitting in rows along the fences, saying nothing, watching the road for someone who does not come.

{remembrance}

A Sending reaches you, and you know the voice before it says anything. The last time you heard it, it was stopping a room from the dais.

{traitor_full} does not greet you. For a while there is only breathing on the other end, as if checking that you are really there.

{traitor_meeting_line}

Then the Sending ends. It does not finish. It is ended, from the other side, like a door pulled shut against a draft.

{remembrance}

The Register lies open on the lectern in the Grand Hall, at the line that stopped at Commencement. {faculty_manner}

'...and by the hand of this Register, the Aldric Academy names {wizard_name} into the discipline of the {declared_plural}.'

The Register writes it as it is spoken, in the hand of {faculty_name}, on a fresh line under the one that stopped: "Be it recorded that the Aldric Academy names {wizard_name} into the discipline of the {declared_plural}." The old line still stops where it stopped. This one finishes.

{intention_callback}

{unmaking_opening}

From the edge of the Anchorhold you watch the reading close. It does not burn or fall. It closes the way water closes over a dropped stone: the kingdoms first, then the roads between them, then the faces you knew, smoothing over until the surface shows nothing at all but the sky, which has already begun to write again.

Behind you the campus is exactly as you left it. The bell's note. The steam over the refectory. Everything you built is still built.

{new_reading_summary}
